# Work section — senior portfolio guidelines

Apply when editing **case study data** (`src/data/case-studies/**/index.json`), **featured work** (`featured-work.tsx`), or **work** pages. Follow `design.md` for typography and layout.

## 1. Structure (reading order)

**Work cards & case study body:** **Problem → Role → Solution → Impact**

| Block    | JSON / UI |
|----------|-----------|
| Problem  | `problem.description`; on cards the **problem line** is carried by `oneLiner` (why it mattered). |
| Role     | `myRole.description` (ownership). |
| Solution | `solution.description` (what was built, high level). |
| Impact   | `impactMetric` (hook, ≤100 chars), `impact.metrics`, `impact.description` (what changed—**last** so it lands). |

**Featured card stack (home index):** **title → `date` → `oneLiner` (problem) → `techTags` → `impactMetric` (impact last) → optional Repository link** (only when `repoUrl` or GitHub-only `liveUrl` exists) **→ CTA.** Do not show the product Live link on featured cards; use the case study page and `/work` for live URLs.

**Case study page:** Render sections **Problem → My role → Solution → Impact**. **Hero:** **title → `date` → `oneLiner` → `techTags` → `liveUrl` / `repoUrl` buttons** (do **not** repeat `impactMetric` in the hero; impact lives in the Impact section). Use `repoUrl` for GitHub; if only `liveUrl` is GitHub, treat it as the repository link in UI.

## 2. Character limits

Count characters on the stored string (including spaces).

| Field | Max |
|-------|-----|
| `problem.description` | ≤ 120 |
| `myRole.description` | ≤ 80 |
| `solution.description` | ≤ 140 |
| `impactMetric` | ≤ 100 |
| `oneLiner` | ≤ 120 |

`impact.metrics`: one idea per bullet; keep each line short. Closing `impact.description`: one tight paragraph; prefer **≤ 100 chars** when possible so impact stays punchy.

## 3. One idea per section

- **Problem:** context only.  
- **Role:** responsibility only.  
- **Solution:** approach only.  
- **Impact:** outcomes only.  
Do not blend sections.

## 4. No tech dumping

- Do not list frameworks or vendors in **problem / role / solution** prose.  
- **Stack belongs in `techTags` only** (and in outcome bullets only when the fact itself is the proof, e.g. store listing).

## 5. Impact still matters most (even when last)

- Make **`impactMetric`** and impact bullets **measurable or meaningful**.  
- Avoid weak vanity metrics (“10 projects built”, “3 apps created”). Prefer ratings, adoption, growth, shipped version, or business signal.

## 6. Ownership

- **Role** copy: lead with **Owned / Led / Built**.  
- Avoid “worked on”, “helped with”.

## 7. Collaboration

- Mention PMs, designers, or company **briefly** when true.  
- Do not dilute ownership.

## 8. Scanning

Short sentences, no filler. A featured card should read in **~5–10 seconds**.

## 9. Visual & proof (critical)

Each case study JSON must include:

- **`date`:** string (e.g. year or ISO-ish label) shown on `/work`, featured cards, and case study hero.  
- **`liveUrl`:** real product / App Store / deployed demo when it exists (not GitHub—use `repoUrl` or GitHub-only handling).  
- **`repoUrl`:** optional; use for GitHub when separate from `liveUrl`.

`/work` rows show **Live** / **Repository** text links when URLs exist, and **`date`** under the title as well as in the date column.

## 10. Consistency

Same section order, tone density, and formatting across all projects under `case-studies/`.

## Core principle

Each project should answer:

> Can this person take ownership, build the solution, and deliver real impact?
